my-id "q-83615" :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\cdot \\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(3-0)^{2}+(5-5)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+9+0+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83615/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d702975-166e-5067-ae3c-1152fade8248"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-83617"] :question/problem "Find the distance between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=\\overset{^}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\overset{^}{x}) & =‖x-\\overset{^}{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\overset{^}{x}}_{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3-2)^{2}+(-3-(-1))^{2}+(0-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-86822/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "02031867-56ed-5133-8c01-f1e09603449c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86822/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "7bf2336e-f67b-5460-ba1f-a924232d54db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86822/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ffabd467-8bd7-584f-81e3-f2b448d8a598" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86822/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "73323716-04f9-519c-b808-b4ec41e851e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86822/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "3c24eb56-65ac-548e-96e6-d48f